# What each entry of valgrind-ct.supp absorbs in one ct.yml run of the
# `ct_flows` harness, per build: `<profile> <count> <suppression name>`.
#
# Valgrind commons errors up by the top four code addresses on their stack,
# so an entry can also absorb later errors its pattern never matched, and
# `--quiet` hides the counts. ct.yml runs Valgrind with `-s`, which lists
# every entry used and its count at exit, and ci/check-ct-suppressions.py
# fails the run unless that list is exactly the one below for the build:
# an entry missing, an entry not listed here (Valgrind's default ones
# included) or a different count all fail it. Every stanza of
# valgrind-ct.supp must appear here for at least one build.
#
# A count should move only when the flows change how often the pattern runs
# on tainted data; change it in the same commit as the flows, and say why.
# Anything else that moves it (an entry absorbing other errors, a dependency
# bump, codegen drift) is what this check is for: explain the new number
# before writing it here, and never copy it from the run being checked.
#
# 184: how many times the invariant `CtOption` assert in p256's OSSWU map
# runs on tainted input in these flows. Debug matches it with the outlined
# entry, release with the inlined one, and each build uses only its own.
debug 184 p256-hash2curve-invariant-ctoption-assert-osswu-outlined-cond
release 184 p256-hash2curve-invariant-ctoption-assert-osswu-cond
